{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>For they are slack, etc.</b> One needs to know who attributed the cry about service to Elohim to the fact that the labor is slack upon them. And perhaps it intends to say that they did not want to go to sacrifice except because they saw that HaShem had dealt well with them, lightening the bondage from upon them so that they were idle; <b>therefore</b>, etc. — meaning, on account of this they cry, saying, ״We will sacrifice,״ etc. — meaning, to bring a thanksgiving offering for the good that He brought them out from the distress of bondage; for otherwise, what goodness of HaShem is upon them that would obligate them to sacrifice to Him? Therefore he said, <b>let the labor be heavy</b> upon them, and from now on they will no longer speak these false words, for even according to their own reasoning they have no cause to sacrifice, since the benefit of the easing of their distress has ceased from upon them." "<b>Further,</b> it intends [to say] that their saying <b>״Let us go and sacrifice,״</b> etc., indicates that their motive is that whatever work they missed from their labor they will make up in reckoning — when they return, they will press themselves to work each day a greater portion than usual until the completion of their task-work that had been missed. Therefore he said, <b>״You shall not gather to give straw,״</b> etc., and the quota of, etc. And the reason is <b>for they are slack, etc.; therefore they cry, saying</b> — meaning, a cry behind which is another saying, namely the repayment of labor that they will do upon their return. If so, <b>let it be heavy</b>, etc. And understand:" "<b>Further,</b> it intends [to say] in His saying <b>and let them not relax</b> — an expression of slackness. And He stated that the cause of the slackness is in the matter that was said to them from Moses, which in Pharaoh's eyes is falsehood. And the intention is along the lines of what I explained in the verse ״והשבתם״ etc., for in the midst of the fear lest He strike them, faintness may enter their hearts and they will not have the strength for the heavy labor that is upon them; therefore, ״let it be heavy,״ etc., as mentioned."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:24:54.508012577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}